From 7a62f20452fb9cf85f762eb961d17c63a7a4a903 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sivan <zifanuu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 00:18:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(mcp): hold the connection generation open during an
 OAuth browser leg
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The initialize request's 60-second timeout fired while the user was
still approving access in the browser: the supervisor closed the
generation — destroying the pending redirectToAuthorization and the
loopback listener — and respawned, restarting the flow from scratch.
The user's approval then landed on a dead callback port, the grant
record kept only the dynamic-registration client information, and every
retry looped through the same race.

The provider now exposes the pending leg (awaitingBrowser / browserLeg),
and the supervisor's failure path holds the generation until the leg
settles: a successful exchange finishes the tool sync in-place inside
the same generation; a failed leg re-enters the existing reconnect
budget. The browser-opener is injected so tests never spawn a real
browser, and the record key folds serverNames like
cloudflare__cloudflare-api into the credential-key grammar instead of
throwing in the provider constructor.
